or Treatment of Logical Structure</head>\r\n<p>When an XML processor encounters a start-tag, it must make\r\nat least the following information available to the application:\r\n<ulist>\r\n<item>\r\n<p>the element type's generic identifier</p>\r\n</item>\r\n<item>\r\n<p>the names of attributes known to apply to this element type\r\n(validating processors must make available names of all attributes\r\ndeclared for the element type; non-validating processors must\r\nmake available at least the names of the attributes for which\r\nvalues are specified.\r\n</p>\r\n</item>\r\n</ulist>\r\n</p>\r\n</div2>\r\n--> \r\n\r\n</div1>\r\n<!-- &Entities; -->\r\n\r\n<div1 id='sec-physical-struct'>\r\n<head>ʪ����¤</head>\r\n \r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id=\"dt-entity\" term=\"Entity\">\r\nXMLʸ��ϡ���İʾ�ε���ñ�̤��鹽�����롣���ε���ñ�̤�<term>����</term>�Ȥ��������Τϡ�<term>����</term>������ʸ�����(�ʹ߻���)�ڤ�<termref def='dt-doctype'>����DTD&subset;</termref>������ơ�<term>̾��</term>��&identified;��\r\n</termdef>\r\n\r\n<!-- Added for CFG -->\r\n<!-- obscurity amputated by TWB -->\r\n<!-- entire sentence amputated by CMSMcQ:  no one but NO ONE is\r\nready for entities declared as\r\n<!ENTITY foo \"http://www.foo.com/bar.xml#id\">\r\nand it's pointless to suggest that it's possible\r\nunder current circumstances. -->\r\n<!-- An entity may be stored in, -->\r\n<!--but need not be coterminous with, -->\r\n<!-- but need not comprise the whole of,  -->\r\n<!-- a single physical storage object such as a file or -->\r\n<!-- database field. -->\r\n<!-- End sentence added for CFG -->��XMLʸ��ϡ�<termref def=\"dt-docent\">ʸ�����</termref>�ȸƤּ��Τ��Ĥ�ġ�<termref def=\"dt-xml-proc\">XML&processor;</termref>�ϡ�����ʸ����Τ�������򳫻Ϥ��롣ʸ����Τ���ʸ��Τ��٤Ƥ�ޤ�Ǥ�褤��</p>\r\n\r\n<p>���Τϡ�&parsed-entity;����&unparsed-entity;�Ȥ��롣<termdef id=\"dt-parsedent\" term=\"Text Entity\"><term>&parsed-entity;</term>�����Ƥϡ�&parsed-entity;��<termref def='dt-repltext'>&replacement-text;</termref>�ȸƤ֡�����<termref def=\"dt-text\">�ƥ�����</termref>�ϡ�ʸ������Τΰ����Ȥ��Ʋ�᤹�롣\r\n</termdef>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id=\"dt-unparsed\" term=\"Unparsed Entity\">\r\n<term>&unparsed-entity;</term>�ϡ����Ƥ�<termref def='dt-text'>�ƥ�����</termref>�Ǥ⤽���Ǥʤ��Ȥ�褤�꥽�����Ȥ��롣�ƥ����Ȥξ�硤XML�Ǥʤ��Ȥ�褤����&unparsed-entity;�ˤϡ�<termref def=\"dt-notation\">��ˡ</termref>����Ϣ�դ���졤���ε�ˡ�ϡ�̾����&identified;����ˡ��̾���ڤӴ�Ϣ�դ���줿&identifier;��XML&processor;��&application;���Ϥ��Ȥ����׷�ʳ��ϡ�XML�ϡ�&unparsed-entity;�����Ƥ����¤��ʤ���\r\n</termdef> \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&parsed-entity;�ϡ����λ��Ȥˤ�ä�̾���ǸƤӽФ���&unparsed-entity;�ϡ�<kw>ENTITY</kw>������<kw>ENTITIES</kw>����°�����ͤȤ��ơ�̾���ǻ��Ȥ��롣</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id='gen-entity' term='general entity'><term>���̼���</term>�ϡ�ʸ�����Ƥ���ǻ��Ѥ���&parsed-entity;�Ȥ��롣�����ޤ��ˤʤ�ʤ��¤ꡤ����&TR-or-Rec;�Ǥϡ����̼��Τ�ñ��<emph>����</emph>�ȸƤ֡�</termdef><termdef id='dt-PE' term='Parameter entity'>�ѥ�᥿���Τϡ�DTD��ǻ��Ѥ���&parsed-entity;�Ȥ��롣</termdef>�����Σ�����μ��Τϡ��ۤʤ�񼰤ǻ��Ȥ����ۤʤ�ʸ̮��ǧ�����롣</p>\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n<div2 id='sec-synchro'>\r\n<head>Logical and Physical Structures</head>\r\n<p>The logical and physical structures (elements and entities)\r\nin an XML document must\r\nbe properly nested.\r\n<termref def='dt-stag'>Tags</termref> and <termref def='dt-element'>elements</termref> must\r\neach begin and end in the same <termref def='dt-entity'>entity</termref>,  but may\r\nrefer to other \r\nentities internally; <termref def='dt-comment'>comments</termref>, \r\n<termref def='dt-pi'>processing instructions</termref>, \r\n<termref def='dt-charref'>character\r\nreferences</termref>, and \r\n<termref def='dt-entref'>entity references</termref> must each be contained entirely\r\nwithin a single entity. Entities must each contain an integral number\r\nof elements, comments, processing instructions, and references,\r\npossibly together with character data not contained within any element\r\nin the entity, or else they must contain non-textual data, which by\r\ndefinition contains no elements.</p></div2>\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<div2 id='sec-references'>\r\n<head>ʸ�����ȵڤӼ��λ���</head>\r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id=\"dt-charref\" term=\"Character Reference\">\r\n<term>ʸ������</term>�ϡ�ISO/IEC 10646ʸ������������ʸ�����㤨�С����ϵ��狼��ľ�������Բ�ǽ��ʸ���򻲾Ȥ��롣\r\n\r\n<scrap lang='ebnf'>\r\n<head>ʸ������</head>\r\n<prod id='NT-CharRef'><lhs>CharRef</lhs>\r\n<rhs>'&amp;#' [0-9]+ ';' </rhs>\r\n<rhs>| '&hcro;' [0-9a-fA-F]+ ';'</rhs>\r\n<wfc def=\"wf-Legalchar\"/>\r\n</prod>\r\n</scrap>\r\n<wfcnote id=\"wf-Legalchar\">\r\n<head>������ʸ��</head>\r\n<p>ʸ�����Ȥǻ��Ȥ���ʸ���ϡ���ü����<termref def=\"NT-Char\">Char</termref>�˽���ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���</p>\r\n</wfcnote>\r\nʸ���� \"<code>&amp;#x</code>\" �ǻϤޤ�С���ü�� \"<code>;</code>\" �ޤǤο����ڤӥ���ե��٥åȤϡ�ISO/IEC 10646 ��ʸ�������ɤ�16�ʿ�ɽ���Ȥ��롣\r\n<!--���ܸ����ˤĤ���: letter�ϥ���ե��٥åȤ��������� ���� -->\r\nʸ���� \"<code>&amp;#</code>\" �ǻϤޤ�С���ü�� \"<code>;</code>\" �ޤǤο����ϡ�ʸ�������ɤ�10�ʿ�ɽ���Ȥ��롣\r\n</termdef>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id=\"dt-entref\" term=\"Entity Reference\">\r\n<term>���λ���</term>�ϡ�̾�����դ������Τ����Ƥ򻲾Ȥ��롣</termdef><termdef id='dt-GERef' term='General Entity Reference'>���̼��Τؤλ��Ȥϡ�����ѥ����(<code>&amp;</code>)�ڤӥ��ߥ�����(<code>;</code>)����ڤ�ҤȤ����Ѥ��롣</termdef><termdef id='dt-PERef' term='Parameter-entity reference'><term>�ѥ�᥿����</term>�ؤλ��Ȥϡ��ѡ�����ȵ���(<code>%</code>)�ڤӥ��ߥ�����(<code>;</code>)����ڤ�ҤȤ����Ѥ��롣\r\n</termdef>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<scrap lang=\"ebnf\">\r\n<head>���λ���</head>\r\n<prod id='NT-Reference'><lhs>Reference</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def='NT-EntityRef'>EntityRef</nt> \r\n| <nt def='NT-CharRef'>CharRef</nt></rhs></prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-EntityRef'><lhs>EntityRef</lhs>\r\n<rhs>'&amp;' <nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt> ';'</rhs>\r\n<wfc def='wf-entdeclared'/>\r\n<vc def='vc-entdeclared'/>\r\n<wfc def='textent'/>\r\n<wfc def='norecursion'/>\r\n</prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-PEReference'><lhs>PEReference</lhs>\r\n<rhs>'%' <nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt> ';'</rhs>\r\n<wfc def='wf-entdeclared'/>\r\n<vc def='vc-entdeclared'/>\r\n<wfc def='textent'/>\r\n<wfc def='norecursion'/>\r\n<wfc def='indtd'/>\r\n</prod>\r\n</scrap>\r\n\r\n<wfcnote id='wf-entdeclared'>\r\n<head>���Τ��������Ƥ��뤳��</head>\r\n<p>DTD��⤿�ʤ�ʸ�񡤥ѥ�᥿���λ��Ȥ�ޤޤʤ�����DTD&subset;��������ʸ������ \"<code>standalone='yes'</code>\" ����ʸ��ˤ����ơ����λ��Ȥ��Ѥ��� <nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt> �ϡ����μ��Τ������Ϳ����̾���ȡ�<termref def=\"dt-match\">&match;</termref>���ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ�����������&well-formed;��ʸ��ϡ�����&magicents; ���������ɬ�פϤʤ����ѥ�᥿���Τξ��ϡ�����ϡ����Ȥ���Ԥ��ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���Ʊ�ͤˡ����̼��Τξ��ϡ�°���ꥹ�������&default-value;��Ǥλ��Ȥ����ˡ����������ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���</p>\r\n\r\n<p>����&subset;���ϳ����ѥ�᥿���ΤǼ��Τ��������Ȥ���&non-validating;&processor;����������ɤߡ��������뤳�Ȥ�<titleref href='include-if-valid'>��̳�Ť��ʤ�</titleref>��������ʸ��Ǥϡ����Τ��������ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ��Ȥ�����§�ϡ�&well-formed;����ǤϤʤ���\r\n</p>\r\n</wfcnote>\r\n\r\n<vcnote id=\"vc-entdeclared\">\r\n<head>���Τ��������Ƥ��뤳��</head>\r\n<p>\r\n����&subset;���ϳ����ѥ�᥿���Τ��äƤ��ơ�\"<code>standalone='no'</code>\"����ʸ��ˤ����ơ����λ��Ȥ��Ѥ��� <nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt> �ϡ����μ��Τ������Ϳ����̾����<termref def=\"dt-match\">&match;</termref>���ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ�����߱������Τ��ᡤ&valid;��ʸ���<titleref href=\"sec-escapes\">���餫��������������Τε���</titleref>�ǻ��ꤷ���񼰤ˤ�äơ����� &magicents;��������뤳�Ȥ�˾�ޤ������ѥ�᥿���Τξ��ϡ�����ϡ����Ȥ���Ԥ��ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���Ʊ�ͤˡ����̼��Τξ��ϡ�°���ꥹ�������&default-value;��Ǥλ��Ȥ�����ˡ����������ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���\r\n</p>\r\n</vcnote>\r\n\r\n<!-- FINAL EDIT:  is this duplication too clumsy? -->\r\n\r\n<wfcnote id='textent'>\r\n<head>&parsed-entity;</head>\r\n<p>\r\n���λ��Ȥϡ�<termref def=\"dt-unparsed\">&unparsed-entity;</termref>��̾����ޤ�Ǥ��ƤϤʤ�ʤ���&unparsed-entity;�ϡ�<kw>ENTITY</kw>������<kw>ENTITIES</kw> ���Ȥ����������<termref def=\"dt-attrval\">°����</termref>�Ȥ��Ƥ������ȤǤ��롣\r\n</p>\r\n</wfcnote>\r\n\r\n<wfcnote id='norecursion'>\r\n<head>�Ƶ��ʤ�</head>\r\n<p>&parsed-entity;�ϡ����켫�Τؤλ��Ȥ�ľ�ܤˤ���ܤˤ�ޤ�ǤϤʤ�ʤ���</p>\r\n</wfcnote>\r\n\r\n<wfcnote id='indtd'>\r\n<head>DTD����</head>\r\n<p>\r\n�ѥ�᥿���λ��Ȥϡ�<termref def='dt-doctype'>DTD</termref>��ˤ������и����Ƥ褤��\r\n<!--\r\nIn the external DTD subset, a parameter-entity reference is \r\nrecognized only at the locations where\r\nthe nonterminal <nt def=\"NT-PEReference\">PEReference</nt> or the\r\nspecial operator <code>%</code> appears in a production of the\r\ngrammar.  In the internal subset, parameter-entity references\r\nare recognized only when they match \r\nthe <nt def=\"NT-InternalPERef\">InternalPERef</nt> non-terminal\r\nin the production for <nt def=\"NT-markupdecl\">markupdecl</nt>.\r\n-->\r\n</p>\r\n</wfcnote>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nʸ�����ȵڤӼ��λ��Ȥ���򡤼��˼�����\r\n<eg>Type &lt;key>less-than&lt;/key> (&hcro;3C;) to save options.\r\nThis document was prepared on &amp;docdate; and\r\nis classified &amp;security-level;.</eg>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n�ѥ�᥿���λ��Ȥ���򡤼��˼�����\r\n<eg>&lt;!ENTITY % ISOLat2\r\n         SYSTEM \"http://www.xml.com/iso/isolat2-xml.entities\" >\r\n%ISOLat2;\r\n</eg>\r\n</p>\r\n</div2>\r\n \r\n<div2 id='sec-entity-decl'>\r\n<head>�������</head>\r\n \r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id=\"dt-entdecl\" term=\"entity declaration\">\r\n���Τϡ����ΤȤ����������롣\r\n<scrap lang='ebnf'>\r\n<head>�������</head>\r\n<prodgroup pcw2=\"5\" pcw4=\"18.5\">\r\n<prod id='NT-EntityDecl'><lhs>EntityDecl</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def=\"NT-GEDecl\">GEDecl</nt></rhs><com>���̼���</com>\r\n<rhs>| <nt def=\"NT-PEDecl\">PEDecl</nt></rhs><com>�ѥ�᥿����</com>\r\n</prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-GEDecl'><lhs>GEDecl</lhs>\r\n<rhs>'&lt;!ENTITY' <nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> <nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> <nt def='NT-EntityDef'>EntityDef</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-S'>S</nt>? '&gt;'</rhs>\r\n</prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-PEDecl'><lhs>PEDecl</lhs>\r\n<rhs>| '&lt;!ENTITY' <nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> '%' <nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt> <nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-PEDef'>PEDef</nt> <nt def='NT-S'>S</nt>? '&gt;'</rhs>\r\n<com>�ѥ�᥿����</com>\r\n</prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-EntityDef'><lhs>EntityDef</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def='NT-EntityValue'>EntityValue</nt>\r\n</rhs>\r\n<!--<wfc def=\"WF-EntityValue\"/>-->\r\n<rhs>| <nt def='NT-ExternalDef'>ExternalDef</nt></rhs>\r\n<!--<wfc def=\"WF-External\"/>-->\r\n</prod>\r\n<!-- FINAL EDIT: what happened to WFs here? -->\r\n<prod id='NT-PEDef'><lhs>PEDef</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def='NT-EntityValue'>EntityValue</nt> \r\n| <nt def='NT-ExternalID'>ExternalID</nt></rhs></prod>\r\n</prodgroup>\r\n</scrap>\r\n\r\n<nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt> �ϡ�<termref def=\"dt-entref\">���λ���</termref>�ˤ����Ƽ��Τ�&identify;��&unparsed-entity;�ʤ�С�<kw>ENTITY</kw> ������<kw>ENTITIES</kw>����°������ǡ����Τ�&identify;��Ʊ��μ��Τ����ʾ���������С��ǽ��������Ѥ��롣&at-user-option;��ʣ��������������Τ˴ؤ���XML&processor;�ϡ��ٹ��Ф��Ƥ�褤��\r\n</termdef>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n<wfcnote id=\"WF-Entityvalue\">\r\n<head>Well-Formed Internal Entity</head>\r\n<p>General entities defined by an <nt\r\ndef=\"NT-EntityValue\">EntityValue</nt> must be well-formed, as defined\r\nin section <specref ref=\"wf-entities\"/>.\r\n</p>\r\n</wfcnote>\r\n<wfcnote id=\"WF-External\">\r\n<head>Well-Formed External Entity</head>\r\n<p>General text entities defined by an <nt\r\ndef=\"NT-ExternalDef\">ExternalDef</nt>, must be well-formed, as defined\r\nin the section on <titleref xml-link=\"simple\"\r\nhref=\"wf-entities\">well-formed entities.</titleref>.</p>\r\n</wfcnote>\r\n--> \r\n\r\n<div3 id='sec-internal-ent'>\r\n<head>��������</head>\r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id='dt-internent' term=\"Internal Entity Replacement Text\">\r\n���Τ������ <nt def='NT-EntityValue'>EntityValue</nt>�ΤȤ��������<term>��������</term>�Ȥ���������ϡ��̸Ĥ�ʪ��Ū����ñ�̤�⤿�������Τ����Ƥϡ�������Ϳ���롣</termdef>������<termref def='dt-repltext'>&replacement-text;</termref>����������ˤϡ�<termref def='dt-litentval'>&literal;������</termref>��Ǥμ��λ��ȵڤ�ʸ�����Ȥν�������ɬ�פȤʤ뤫�⤷��ʤ����Ȥ����դ��롣�ܺ٤ϡ�<titleref href='intern-replacement'>�������Τ�&replacement-text;�ι���</titleref>�򻲾ȡ�\r\n\r\n<!-- redundant -TWB\r\nWithin the <nt def=\"NT-EntityValue\">EntityValue</nt>,\r\nparameter-entity references and character references are recognized\r\nand expanded immediately. \r\nGeneral-entity references within the\r\nreplacement text are not recognized\r\nat the time the entity declaration is parsed, though they may be\r\nrecognized when the entity itself is referred to.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n�������Τϡ�<termref def=\"dt-parsedent\">&parsed-entity;</termref>�Ȥ��롣\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>���������������򡤼��˼�����\r\n<eg>&lt;!ENTITY Pub-Status \"This is a pre-release of the specification.\"></eg></p>\r\n</div3>\r\n \r\n<div3 id='sec-external-ent'>\r\n<head>��������</head>\r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id=\"dt-extent\" term=\"External Entity\">\r\n���Τ��������ΤǤʤ���С�<term>��������</term>�Ȥ������ΤȤ����������롣\r\n\r\n<scrap lang='ebnf'>\r\n<head>�����������</head>\r\n<prod id='NT-ExternalDef'><lhs>ExternalDef</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def='NT-ExternalID'>ExternalID</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-NDataDecl'>NDataDecl</nt>?</rhs></prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-ExternalID'><lhs>ExternalID</lhs>\r\n<rhs>'SYSTEM' <nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-SystemLiteral'>SystemLiteral</nt></rhs>\r\n<rhs>| 'PUBLIC' <nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-PubidLiteral'>PubidLiteral</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-SystemLiteral'>SystemLiteral</nt>\r\n</rhs>\r\n</prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-NDataDecl'><lhs>NDataDecl</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> 'NDATA' <nt def='NT-S'>S</nt> \r\n<nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt></rhs>\r\n<vc def='not-declared'/></prod>\r\n</scrap>\r\n\r\n<nt def='NT-NDataDecl'>NDataDecl</nt> ��¸�ߤ���С����μ��Τϡ�<termref def=\"dt-unparsed\">&unparsed-entity;</termref>�Ȥ��������Ǥʤ���С�&parsed-entity;�Ȥ��롣</termdef>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<vcnote id='not-declared'>\r\n<head>��ˡ���������Ƥ��뤳��</head>\r\n<p>\r\n<nt def='NT-Name'>Name</nt> �ϡ��������<termref def=\"dt-notation\">��ˡ</termref>��̾����&match;���ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���\r\n</p>\r\n</vcnote>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id=\"dt-sysid\" term=\"System Identifier\">\r\n������� <kw>SYSTEM</kw> �θ�� <nt def='NT-SystemLiteral'>SystemLiteral</nt> �򡤼��Τ�<term>�����ƥ�&identifier;</term>�ȸƤ֡������URI�Ȥ������μ��Τ����Ƥ���Ф��Τ��Ѥ��Ƥ�褤��</termdef>URI�ȶ��˻Ȥ����Ȥ�¿���ϥå���(\"<code>#</code>\")�ڤӥե饰����&identifier;�ϡ������ˤϡ�URI���Τΰ����ȤϤ��ʤ����ե饰����&identifier;���������ƥ�&identifier;����ʬ�Ȥ���Ϳ�����Ƥ����硤XML&processor;�ϡ�&error;��Ф��Ƥ�褤������&TR-or-Rec;���ϰϳ��ξ���(�㤨�С����������DTD�����̤�XML�������������&application;�λ��ͤˤ�ä�������줿����̿��)�ˤ�äƾ�񤭤���ʤ��¤ꡤ����Ū��URI�ϡ����μ��Τΰ��֡����ʤ�������μ��Τ����������ե����������Ū�Ȥ��롣�������äơ�DTD������&subset;�ˤ����������Ǥ�����Ū��URI�ϡ�ʸ��ΰ��֤ˤĤ�������Ū�Ȥ��롣����&subset;�ˤ����������Ǥ�����Ū��URI�ϡ����γ���&subset;��ޤ�ե�����ΰ��֤�����Ū�Ȥ��롣\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<termdef id=\"dt-pubid\" term=\"Public identifier\">\r\n�����ƥ�&identifier;�ʳ��ˡ��������Τϡ�<term>����&identifier;</term>��ޤ�Ǥ�褤��\r\n</termdef>\r\n���Τ����Ƥ���Ф�XML&processor;�ϡ����θ���&identifier;���Ѥ��ơ������URI���������ߤƤ�褤��XML&processor;������˼��Ԥ������ϡ������ƥ�&literal;�Ȥ��ƻ��ꤷ��URI���Ѥ��ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���&match;�������ˡ�����&identifier;��ˤ������ʸ������ʤ�&string;�ϡ����٤�ñ���&space-character;(#x20)�����������ʤ���Фʤ餺������ζ���ʸ���Ϻ�����ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>���������������򡤼��˼�����\r\n<eg>&lt;!ENTITY open-hatch\r\n         SYSTEM \"http://www.textuality.com/boilerplate/OpenHatch.xml\">\r\n&lt;!ENTITY open-hatch\r\n         PUBLIC \"-//Textuality//TEXT Standard open-hatch boilerplate//EN\"\r\n         \"http://www.textuality.com/boilerplate/OpenHatch.xml\">\r\n&lt;!ENTITY hatch-pic\r\n         SYSTEM \"../grafix/OpenHatch.gif\"\r\n         NDATA gif ></eg></p>\r\n</div3>\r\n \r\n</div2>\r\n\r\n<div2 id='TextEntities'>\r\n<head>&parsed-entity;</head>\r\n<div3 id='sec-TextDecl'>\r\n<head>�ƥ��������</head>\r\n<p>����&parsed-entity;�ϡ�<term>�ƥ��������</term>�ǻϤޤäƤ�褤��\r\n<scrap lang='ebnf'>\r\n<head>�ƥ��������</head>\r\n<prodgroup pcw4=\"12.5\" pcw5=\"13\">\r\n<prod id='NT-TextDecl'><lhs>TextDecl</lhs>\r\n<rhs>&xmlpio; \r\n<nt def='NT-VersionInfo'>VersionInfo</nt>?\r\n<nt def='NT-EncodingDecl'>EncodingDecl</nt>\r\n<nt def='NT-S'>S</nt>? &pic;</rhs>\r\n<!-- <wfc def='wfc-xmldecliteral'/> -->\r\n<!-- <wfc def='wfc-no-nonleading-encdec'/> -->\r\n</prod>\r\n</prodgroup>\r\n</scrap>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>�ƥ���������ϡ����Τޤޤη��Ǹ���ʤ���Фʤ餺��&parsed-entity;�ؤλ��Ȥ��ͳ���ƤϤʤ�ʤ����Ȥ����դ��롣</p>\r\n<p>����&parsed-entity;�ˤ����ơ��ƥ���������ϡ���Ƭ�ʳ��Τ����ʤ���֤ˤ�и����ʤ���</p>\r\n</div3>\r\n<div3 id='wf-entities'>\r\n<head>&well-formed;��&parsed-entity;</head>\r\n<p>��٥�<nt def='NT-document'>document</nt>����������§��&match;����С�ʸ����Τϡ�&well-formed;�Ȥ��롣��٥�<nt def='NT-ExtParsedEnt'>ExtParsedEnt</nt>����������§��&match;����С������ΰ���&parsed-entity;�ϡ�&well-formed;�Ȥ��롣��٥�<nt def='NT-ExtPE'>ExtPE</nt>����������§��&match;����С������ѥ�᥿���Τϡ�&well-formed;�Ȥ��롣\r\n\r\n<scrap lang='ebnf'>\r\n<head>&well-formed;��&parsed-entity;</head>\r\n<prod id='NT-ExtParsedEnt'><lhs>ExtParsedEnt</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def='NT-TextDecl'>TextDecl</nt>? \r\n<nt def='NT-content'>content</nt></rhs>\r\n</prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-ExtPE'><lhs>ExtPE</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def='NT-TextDecl'>TextDecl</nt>? \r\n<nt def='NT-extSubset'>extSubset</nt></rhs>\r\n</prod>\r\n</scrap>\r\n&replacement-text;������٥�<nt def='NT-content'>content</nt>����������§��&match;����С������ΰ���&parsed-entity;�ϡ�&well-formed;�Ȥ��롣DTD��Ǹ�ޤ��ɤ߹��ޤʤ��ȡ��μ¤ˤ����Ƚ��Ǥ��ʤ����Ȥ����ա����٤Ƥ������Υѥ�᥿���Τϡ�����ˤ�ä�&well-formed;�Ȥ��롣\r\n</p>\r\n<p>���Τ�&well-formed;�ʷ�̤Ȥ��ơ�XMLʸ�������Ū�ڤ�ʪ��Ū��¤�ϡ�����������ҤȤʤ롣<termref def='dt-stag'>���ϥ���</termref>��<termref def='dt-etag'>��λ����</termref>��<termref def=\"dt-empty\">�����ǥ���</termref>��<termref def='dt-element'>����</termref>��<termref def='dt-comment'>������</termref>��<termref def='dt-pi'>����̿��</termref>��<termref def='dt-charref'>ʸ������</termref>�ڤ�<termref def='dt-entref'>���λ���</termref>������Ĥμ��Τǳ��Ϥ����̤μ��Τǽ�λ���뤳�ȤϤʤ���</p>\r\n</div3>\r\n<div3 id='charencoding'>\r\n<head>���Τˤ�����ʸ����沽</head>\r\n \r\n<p>XMLʸ����γ���&parsed-entity;�ϡ��ơ����̤�ʸ����沽�������Ѥ��Ƥ�褤�����٤Ƥ�XML&processor;�ϡ�UTF-8����沽�������Ρ�UTF-16����沽�������Τ�����Ǥ��ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���\r\n<!--\r\nIt is recognized that for some purposes, the use of additional\r\nISO/IEC 10646 planes other than the Basic Multilingual Plane\r\nmay be required.  \r\nA facility for handling characters in these planes is therefore a\r\ndesirable characteristic in XML processors and applications.\r\n-->\r\n</p>\r\n<p>UTF-16����沽�������Τϡ�ISO/IEC 10646����ϿE�ڤ�Unicode����ϿB�ǵ��ꤹ��&byte-order-mark;(ZERO WIDTH NO-BREAK SPACEʸ����#xFEFF)�ǻϤޤ�ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ�������ϡ���沽��ɸ���Ǥ��äơ�XMLʸ���&markup;�ΰ����Ǥ⡤ʸ���ǡ����ΰ����Ǥ�ʤ���XML&processor;�ϡ�UTF-8����沽����ʸ���UTF-16����沽����ʸ��Ȥζ��̤�Ԥ�����ˡ�����ʸ������Ѳ�ǽ�Ǥʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���</p>\r\n<p>XML&processor;�ϡ�UTF-8�ڤ�UTF-16����沽�������Τ������ɤळ�Ȥ�ɬ�ܤȤ��뤬��¾����沽�������Ǥ��Ѥ��Ƥ��ꡤ��������沽���Ѥ�����Τ�XML&processor;�������Ǥ��뤳�Ȥ�˾�ޤ�����UTF-8����UTF-16�ʳ�����沽�������Ѥ��Ƴ�Ǽ����&parsed-entity;�ϡ���沽�����ޤ�<titleref href='TextDecl'>�ƥ��������</titleref>�ǻϤ�ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���\r\n<scrap lang='ebnf'>\r\n<head>��沽���</head>\r\n<prod id='NT-EncodingDecl'><lhs>EncodingDecl</lhs>\r\n<rhs><nt def=\"NT-S\">S</nt>\r\n'encoding' <nt def='NT-Eq'>Eq</nt> \r\n'\"' <nt def='NT-EncName'>EncName</nt> '\"' | \"'\" \r\n<nt def='NT-EncName'>EncName</nt> \"'\"\r\n</rhs>\r\n</prod>\r\n<prod id='NT-EncName'><lhs>EncName</lhs>\r\n<rhs>[A-Za-z] ([A-Za-z0-9._] | '-')*</rhs>\r\n<com>��ƥ�ʸ��������ޤ���沽̾</com>\r\n</prod>\r\n</scrap>\r\n<termref def='dt-docent'>ʸ�����</termref>�Ǥϡ���沽����ϡ�<termref def=\"dt-xmldecl\">XML���</termref>�ΰ����Ȥ��롣<nt def=\"NT-EncName\">EncName</nt>�ϡ����Ѥ�����沽������̾���Ȥ��롣\r\n</p>\r\n<!-- FINAL EDIT:  check name of IANA and charset names -->\r\n<p>��沽����Ǥϡ���<code>UTF-8</code>��<code>UTF-16</code>��<code>ISO-10646-UCS-2</code>�ڤ�<code>ISO-10646-UCS-4</code>�ϡ�Unicode�ڤ�ISO/IEC 10646�γƼ���沽�Τ�����Ѥ��롣��<code>ISO-8859-1</code>����<code>ISO-8859-9</code>�ޤǤϡ�ISO 8859���б�����ѡ��ȤΤ�����Ѥ��롣��<code>ISO-2022-JP</code>��<code>Shift_JIS</code>�ڤ�<code>EUC-JP</code>�ϡ�JIS X-0208-1997�γƼ���沽�Τ�����Ѥ��롣XML&processor;�ϡ�����ʳ�����沽������ǧ�����Ƥ�褤��Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA)�ˡ�(<emph>charset</emph>s�Ȥ���)��Ͽ���줿ʸ����沽�����ˤĤ��Ƥϡ������ʳ��ˤĤ��Ƥ⡤��Ͽ���줿̾���ǻ��Ȥ��뤳�Ȥ�˾�ޤ�������������Ͽ���줿̾���ϡ���ʸ������ʸ���ζ��̤򤻤����������Ƥ���Τǡ��������Ф�����Ӥ��ߤ�&processor;�ϡ���ʸ������ʸ���ζ��̤򤷤ʤ���ˡ��Ȥ�Τ�˾�ޤ������Ȥ����դ��롣</p>\r\n<p>XML�����Ϥ��Ϥ��줿���Τ�����沽�����ޤ�ˤ⤫����餺������Ǽ�������ΰʳ�����������沽����Ƥ����ꡤ��沽��������������Τκǽ�ʳ��ΰ��֤˽и�����С�<termref def=\"dt-error\">&error;</termref>�Ȥ��롣\r\n</p>\r\n<p>&byte-order-mark;�Ǥ���沽����Ǥ�Ϥޤ�ʤ����Τϡ�UTF-8��沽�Ǥʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���</p>\r\n\r\n<p><!-- XML processors should make an effort to use all available\r\ninformation, internal and external, to aid in detecting an entity's correct\r\nencoding.  Such information may include, but is not limited to:\r\n<ulist><item><p>An HTTP header</p></item>\r\n<item><p>A MIME header obtained other than through HTTP</p></item>\r\n<item><p>Metadata provided by the native OS file system or by document\r\nmanagement software</p></item>\r\n<item><p>The bit patterns at the front of an entity, which may\r\nbe analyzed to determine if\r\nthe application of any known encoding yields a valid encoding\r\ndeclaration.  See <titleref href='sec-guessing'>the appendix on\r\nautodetection of character sets</titleref> \r\nfor a fuller description.</p></item></ulist> -->\r\n�����Ǥ��ʤ���沽���ä����Τ�XML&processor;��ȯ�������Ȥ��ϡ�&application;�ˤ��λ��¤����Τ���<termref def='dt-fatal'>&fatal-error;</termref>�Ȥ��ơ�������λ���ʤ���Фʤ�ʤ���\r\n<!--\r\ninform the application of this fact and \r\nmay \r\nallow the application to\r\nrequest either that the entity should be treated as an <termref\r\ndef=\"dt-unparsed\">unparsed entity</termref>, or that processing should\r\ncease.-->\r\n</p>\r\n<p>��沽�������򡤼��˼�����\r\n<eg>&lt;?xml encoding='UTF-8'?>\r\n&lt;?xml encoding='EUC-JP'?></eg></p>\r\n</div3>\r\n</div2>\r\n<div2 id='entproc'>\r\n<head>XML&processor;�ˤ����εڤӻ��Ȥΰ���</head>\r\n<p>����ɽ�ϡ�ʸ�����ȡ����λ��ȵڤ�&unparsed-entity;�θƽФ��������ʸ̮�ڤӳơ��ξ��ˤ�����<termref def='dt-xml-proc'>XML&processor;</termref>���׵᤹�뿶�񤤤����󤹤롣���ֺ�����